  "Question": "I’m thinking of two whole numbers. Their product is \\(24\\) and their sum is \\(11.\\) What is the larger number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since their product is \\(24\\), both whole numbers must be positive. The factor pairs, with the smaller number first, are\n\\[\n(1,24),\\quad (2,12),\\quad (3,8),\\quad (4,6).\n\\]\nThese are all the pairs: if both numbers were at least \\(5\\), their product would be at least \\(25\\).\n\nThe pairs have sums \\(25,14,11,10\\), respectively. Only \\(3\\) and \\(8\\) have sum \\(11\\), so the larger number is \\(8\\), choice D.",
